. 
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 *
. 
.         * We assume that a scale ranging from very right to very left (attitu
> de_scale_01) is a good measure of right vs. left-leaning political preference
> s (hypothesis 2), 
.         * if having a daughter, the respondent is more likely to have left-le
> aning political preferences (score higher on the leftist scale).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with `revlefti
> st' as the dependent variable and the dummy variable `d_daughter' as the inde
> pendent variable
.         
. reg revleftist d_daughter  

      Source |       SS           df       MS      Number of obs   =        85
-------------+----------------------------------   F(1, 83)        =      1.20
       Model |  2.97294118         1  2.97294118   Prob > F        =    0.2767
    Residual |      205.78        83  2.47927711   R-squared       =    0.0142
-------------+----------------------------------   Adj R-squared   =    0.0024
       Total |  208.752941        84  2.48515406   Root MSE        =    1.5746

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  revleftist | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |       -.38   .3470188    -1.10   0.277    -1.070206    .3102064
       _cons |       5.38   .2226781    24.16   0.000     4.937102    5.822898
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. reg revleftist d_daughter, cluster(hid) 

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =         85
                                                F(1, 54)          =       0.71
                                                Prob > F          =     0.4030
                                                R-squared         =     0.0142
                                                Root MSE          =     1.5746

                                   (Std. err. adjusted for 55 clusters in hid)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
  revleftist | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |       -.38   .4508278    -0.84   0.403    -1.283855    .5238553
       _cons |       5.38   .2000056    26.90   0.000     4.979013    5.780987
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation based of directionality and p-value
.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

.         
. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
